Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix:=20=F0=9F=8E=A5=20stop=20the=20camera=20sna?=
 =?UTF-8?q?pping=20186px=20the=20tick=20a=20gate=20opens?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three transition defects, all verified against the sim before touching it:

1. Gate open snapped the camera. _step_gates runs BEFORE _step_camera in the
   same tick, so the gate's camera hold vanished and the ratchet took the whole
   50-186px backlog in one uninterpolated jump. In 2P the trailing player was
   then teleported the same distance by the next tick's _clamp_actor — onto
   whatever was there, mines included. The ratchet is now rate-limited to
   MAX_CAM_STEP (2x PLAYER_SPEED), which still out-runs every actor on the
   field (TANK_SPEED is 0.8x) so it always catches up.

2. The Colossus opened the finale from off-screen with no locator. It spawns at
   final_gate.y - 120 while that never-opening gate pins camera_top to
   final_gate.y - 60, so only its barrels peek in while it sprays aimed
   bullets. The off-screen boss chevron iterated gate bosses and endless_boss
   but not sim.colossus — it does now (view-only, golden-free). Also deleted
   the dead observer branch next to it: osy was a constant +14px tested for
   < 0, so it never fired, and the observer is pinned to camera_top and can't
   go off-screen anyway.

3. 2P: the leader dragged the trailing player into the bottom clamp. Focus is
   min(y) over alive players and _clamp_actor was unconditional, so P2 lost
   vertical control entirely. The trailing player now LIMITS the camera
   instead. Dead partners drop out of the leash, so a downed player can never
   freeze the scroll.

Goldens re-recorded — all six campaign samples moved (measured); endless
verified unchanged. Why-note in test_determinism.gd.
