+## 2026-07-25 -- CAMERA TRANSITION AUDIT: campaign GOLDEN RE-RECORDED.
+## MEASURED, not assumed: ALL SIX campaign samples moved; ENDLESS_GOLDEN VERIFIED
+## UNCHANGED (re-measured with these values committed -- the endless torture wipes
+## at wave 2 and its camera never leaves the ratchet's dead zone).
+## Two changes in _step_camera, both of which bite in the very first seconds of a
+## 2P run, which is why sample 0 moves too:
+##   (1) MAX_CAM_STEP rate-limits the ratchet. A gate opening dropped its camera
+##       hold in ONE tick and the ratchet took the whole 50-186px backlog in that
+##       tick -- an uninterpolated snap, and (2P) a same-distance teleport of the
+##       trailing player on the next tick's _clamp_actor, potentially onto an
+##       armed mine. The camera now moves at most 2x PLAYER_SPEED per tick, so it
+##       still out-runs any actor on the field but spreads the catch-up over ~40
+##       ticks. Every camera_top value along a catch-up differs -> whole stream.
+##   (2) The trailing 2P player LEASHES the camera (desired is limited to
+##       p.y - CAMERA_BAND_BOTTOM for each ALIVE player) instead of being shoved
+##       north by _clamp_actor. In the 2P torture script the two players separate
+##       constantly, so the leash engages within the first sample window and every
+##       subsequent player/enemy position shifts with it. Dead players drop out of
+##       the leash, so a downed partner cannot freeze the scroll.
+## Solo campaign is unaffected by (2) by construction (CAMERA_LEAD 260 sits inside
+## the 344 band); (1) affects solo only at a gate open.
